# Dependabot PR Workflow (Cursor adapter)

**Canonical process:** [docs/guides/dependabot-process.md](../../docs/guides/dependabot-process.md).
Command entry: [`.claude/commands/handle-dependabot.md`](../../.claude/commands/handle-dependabot.md).
Do **not** duplicate the full queue / validation / merge procedure here.

## When this rule loads

Use it when the user asks to handle/process Dependabot PRs, update dependencies via Dependabot, or triage the bot queue. Run the **autonomous** queue from the guide end-to-end without per-PR confirmation; stop only on blockers (failed CI, conflicts after rebase, risky/RN-upgrade PRs).

## Hard constraints (do not weaken)

1. **Authors only:** `app/dependabot` / `dependabot[bot]`; base branch `main`.
2. **Never push agent work to `main`** — squash-merge existing Dependabot PRs only; agent fixes need a ticketed PR ([delivery.mdc](./delivery.mdc)).
3. **One lockfile merge at a time** → wait for `main` CI green → `@dependabot rebase` remaining bots in parallel.
4. **Safe** (lockfile-only / non-native patch; Actions SHA with Action pins green): CI-first when required checks are green.
5. **Risky** / native / Expo: local `npm ci` + `doctor` + full gates from [commands.mdc](./commands.mdc) (incl. `architecture-guard`) + Android smoke.
6. **Do not merge** RN line upgrades / ignored majors without a dedicated ticket (or confirmed ignore).
7. Resolution-log catch-up lands via a **ticketed chore PR**, never a commit on `main`.
